# H, THE HOLDER MATRIX: who bears the remainder, and how much of it. One row per
# (filing, layer, kind), which is the sparse form of an L x 5 matrix. No row means that
# kind bears nothing -- or that nobody said. The two readings are not separated here, which
# is what `share_absent` is for.
#
# ⭐⭐ A DISTRIBUTION AND NOT A SELECTION. One remainder routinely lands on several parties
#    at once: the firm books part of it, a counterparty absorbs part under contract, and a
#    customer waits for the rest. A single "who absorbs this" column would have forced the
#    filer to pick one, and picking one is the flattening the tall table refuses.
#
# ⛔ `counterparty` IS THE ONLY KIND THAT NAMES A PARTY AND A DATE, because it is the only
#   one whose bearer is a third party with an agreement behind it. The schema enforces both
#   directions of that: no other kind may name one, and a counterparty must.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:holder; kind is pm:HolderKind.
SELECT h.filing, h.layer, h.kind,
       h.share_low, h.share_mode, h.share_high, h.share_unit, h.share_absent,
       h.party, h.as_of
FROM pm.holder h
